1
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:06,810
Wait! Wait!

2
00:00:07,050 --> 00:00:10,130
Hey, now! You're going to fall
if you keep running like that!

3
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:13,750
Are you okay, Onii-chan?

4
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:17,410
See? I told you.

5
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:19,870
Come on, let me see.

6
00:00:27,540 --> 00:00:29,880
Shige! Stop that!

7
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,590
What the heck?

8
00:00:46,580 --> 00:00:49,440
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

9
00:00:49,440 --> 00:00:52,250
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

10
00:00:52,250 --> 00:00:55,100
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

11
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,160
(Get ready!)

12
00:00:57,060 --> 00:01:01,750
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

13
00:01:02,810 --> 00:01:07,490
You're a MOB. Can't you feel your own frustration?

14
00:01:08,520 --> 00:01:13,240
Coming down, could you fill your satisfaction?

15
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:17,800
You're a MOB. What do you want to be?

16
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:24,340
Wear your overflowing emotions on your sleeve and break it down

17
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:29,240
What do you see once you go beyond your limits?

18
00:01:29,240 --> 00:01:32,220
(99.9! 99.9!)

19
00:01:32,220 --> 00:01:35,100
The mysterious percentage.

20
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:39,570
Cryin' my life, cryin' my psyche,

21
00:01:39,570 --> 00:01:42,520
cryin' my heart in such commonplaces!

22
00:01:42,520 --> 00:01:45,350
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind?

23
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:48,260
It all begins when it hits 100.

24
00:01:48,260 --> 00:01:51,050
The MOB is alive. The MOB is high.

25
00:01:51,050 --> 00:01:53,940
The MOB is staying frustrated, aren't you?

26
00:01:53,940 --> 00:01:58,330
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind? Right now...

27
00:01:59,650 --> 00:02:00,870
Your life is your own.

28
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:03,640
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

29
00:02:03,310 --> 00:02:08,150
Mob Psycho

30
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:06,530
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

31
00:02:06,530 --> 00:02:09,400
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

32
00:02:09,400 --> 00:02:10,710
(Get ready!)

33
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:17,990
Even Then
~Continue Forward~

34
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:23,370
Now Mob-kun even has a building in his name.

35
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:28,620
Psycho Helmet Religion

36
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:26,580
Even though the Psycho Helmet Religion
has yet to find its leader,

37
00:02:26,580 --> 00:02:28,620
it now has over 700 members.

38
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:32,420
Psycho Helmet Religion

39
00:02:28,860 --> 00:02:32,090
Due to an anonymous donation,
they were able to create a headquarters

40
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:35,380
and its followers are working hard,
day after day, to recruit more followers.

41
00:02:36,480 --> 00:02:40,340
They have no form of scripture
nor really any idea what to do.

42
00:02:40,340 --> 00:02:43,400
All they know is that their beloved founder
is apparently a real esper

43
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:45,430
and in middle school.

44
00:02:45,430 --> 00:02:50,140
Psycho Helmet Religion

45
00:02:45,660 --> 00:02:47,600
The religion is also gaining popularity

46
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,140
and spreading on the internet
as a meme religion.

47
00:02:50,820 --> 00:02:56,350
If Mob-kun finally appears,
this order will get even bigger.

48
00:02:56,760 --> 00:02:57,960
I want to see it happen!

49
00:02:58,510 --> 00:03:01,330
Because... It seems like it'd be fun.

50
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:05,830
It's finally that time of year again.

51
00:03:05,830 --> 00:03:08,770
The annual marathon is here.

52
00:03:07,290 --> 00:03:09,500
In 10 days
Salt Middle School All-Student
Marathon Contest

53
00:03:09,690 --> 00:03:11,620
Seriously?

54
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:14,960
No way! We have to run 5 kilometers again?

55
00:03:11,980 --> 00:03:15,880
Don't even try faking any sickness.
I'll see right through it!

56
00:03:20,860 --> 00:03:22,050
Mob-kun.

57
00:03:22,310 --> 00:03:24,290
Mezato-san? What is it?

58
00:03:24,290 --> 00:03:26,940
There's something I want to talk to you about.

59
00:03:26,940 --> 00:03:29,590
Could you come to the roof during lunch?

60
00:03:29,590 --> 00:03:31,270
It's really important.

61
00:03:31,270 --> 00:03:37,980
Middle School Math

62
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:33,330
I'll be waiting for you.

63
00:03:34,530 --> 00:03:35,720
Shigeo...

64
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,980
Maybe you're going to get asked out again!

65
00:03:38,440 --> 00:03:39,960
For real this time!

66
00:03:39,960 --> 00:03:42,490
No, I'm sure she just wants to talk.

67
00:03:42,490 --> 00:03:44,910
You're too dramatic, Dimple.

68
00:03:45,090 --> 00:03:48,160
Lame! What happened to
that innocent boy I used to know?

69
00:03:48,470 --> 00:03:53,470
Just the other day, you'd get beet red
and flustered simply from talking to a girl.

70
00:03:55,540 --> 00:03:56,960
You see, Mob-kun...

71
00:03:58,070 --> 00:04:00,300
About the marathon...

72
00:04:00,690 --> 00:04:03,950
O-Oh, okay. It's about the marathon...

73
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:06,760
What? Was he actually expecting more?

74
00:04:07,180 --> 00:04:09,270
Why don't you use your powers

75
00:04:09,270 --> 00:04:13,230
to win by a landslide and surprise
the heck out of all the people watching?

76
00:04:13,480 --> 00:04:14,380
Why would I do that?

77
00:04:14,910 --> 00:04:18,440
Well, there's this fan club
that's been looking for you.

78
00:04:18,840 --> 00:04:19,710
Fans?

79
00:04:19,710 --> 00:04:22,580
It's a religious group called Psycho Helmet.

80
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:24,070
Oh, it's a religious group.

81
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:26,070
We're looking for our god.

82
00:04:24,070 --> 00:04:26,070
Psycho Helmet Religion

83
00:04:24,770 --> 00:04:26,070
Oh, it's that.

84
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:29,540
During the press conference the other day...

85
00:04:29,840 --> 00:04:33,610
Apparently, there was a split-second shot
of you from behind.

86
00:04:33,610 --> 00:04:34,620
They analyzed the footage

87
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:37,910
and found out that your uniform
was from Salt Middle School.

88
00:04:38,630 --> 00:04:43,990
The followers are positive that
the poltergeist incident wasn't a fake.

89
00:04:44,830 --> 00:04:48,520
They're likely going to come observe
the area on the day of the marathon.

90
00:04:48,920 --> 00:04:53,520
That's when you'll reveal that
you're the leader they've been looking for!

91
00:04:53,910 --> 00:04:57,730
Don't you want to make that
important moment as dramatic as possible?

92
00:04:58,100 --> 00:05:01,010
Sorry, but I'm going to run
using my own physical strength.

93
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:02,860
I'm even jogging now,

94
00:05:02,860 --> 00:05:06,950
so maybe by next year I'll be able
to place within the top ten.

95
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:10,780
Wow... You actually thought
about it that much?

96
00:05:10,780 --> 00:05:12,870
Who knew you actually had a goal?

97
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:15,350
It can't be next year!

98
00:05:15,350 --> 00:05:17,770
We'll have our high school
entrance exams next year!

99
00:05:17,770 --> 00:05:20,540
We won't have time to deal
with stuff like this anymore!

100
00:05:20,820 --> 00:05:23,280
That's right. Oh, no...

101
00:05:23,280 --> 00:05:24,130
What's up?

102
00:05:25,370 --> 00:05:29,030
If I placed in the top ten
of next year's marathon,

103
00:05:29,560 --> 00:05:32,530
I was planning on asking
Tsubomi-chan out...

104
00:05:32,530 --> 00:05:33,990
S-Say what?

105
00:05:33,990 --> 00:05:35,600
What? Takane-san?!

106
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:39,040
I messed up during the student
council president election,

107
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:42,400
but I wanted to show her how cool
I could be at next year's marathon.

108
00:05:42,910 --> 00:05:44,180
Shigeo...

109
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:48,610
How were you able to change
so much without my noticing?

110
00:05:49,040 --> 00:05:51,580
If next year doesn't work,
it'll have to be this year.

111
00:05:51,870 --> 00:05:55,700
I'll just have to place in the top ten
in the marathon next week!

112
00:05:57,750 --> 00:06:00,210
Telepathy Club

113
00:05:57,750 --> 00:06:00,210
Body Improvement Club

114
00:06:00,210 --> 00:06:03,340
No way! That's the last thing
I thought I'd hear you say.

115
00:06:03,340 --> 00:06:05,670
Do you even remember
where you finished last year?

116
00:06:05,860 --> 00:06:07,680
291st...

117
00:06:07,680 --> 00:06:09,090
You're way too slow!

118
00:06:09,090 --> 00:06:14,850
Strengthening month!!

119
00:06:09,280 --> 00:06:11,790
You finished in the bottom ten.

120
00:06:11,790 --> 00:06:14,850
How are you going to remedy
that in just ten days?

121
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:19,270
Monthly
Muscle

122
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:19,270
Five kilometers is a pretty
rough distance, too.

123
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:22,360
My older brother does track in high school.

124
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:24,050
Should I ask him for some tips?

125
00:06:24,050 --> 00:06:27,490
Last-minute advice isn't going to
turn him into a speedster!

126
00:06:27,680 --> 00:06:31,670
Maybe watch what you eat
and tone your body a bit...

127
00:06:31,670 --> 00:06:33,330
We're not talking about a diet here!

128
00:06:33,570 --> 00:06:36,120
Oh, I know. Why not buy
some fancy running shoes?

129
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,660
You think he has that kind of money?

130
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:39,830
I'll have to give it my all...

131
00:06:39,830 --> 00:06:41,890
That's exactly right, Kageyama!

132
00:06:43,420 --> 00:06:45,270
That's why you're our shadow leader!

133
00:06:45,270 --> 00:06:48,260
The methods and their efficiency don't matter!

134
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:51,310
What matters is whether
you wanna do this or not!

135
00:06:49,590 --> 00:06:54,300
Monthly Muscle

136
00:06:51,590 --> 00:06:54,300
You understand that!

137
00:06:54,300 --> 00:06:54,600
Put on muscle

138
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:54,720
Put on muscle

139
00:06:54,710 --> 00:06:56,250
However, Kageyama...

140
00:06:54,720 --> 00:06:54,850
Put on muscle

141
00:06:54,850 --> 00:06:54,970
Put on muscle

142
00:06:54,970 --> 00:06:59,230
Put on muscle

143
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:59,600
Giving something your all ain't easy.

144
00:06:59,230 --> 00:06:59,310
Put on muscle

145
00:06:59,310 --> 00:06:59,440
Put on muscle

146
00:06:59,890 --> 00:07:03,280
Do you have what it takes
to really put everything on the line?

147
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:05,070
I... I do.

148
00:07:07,070 --> 00:07:08,740
Then you can have my running shoes.

149
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:10,900
What? But they're brand new!

150
00:07:11,140 --> 00:07:12,740
You're just going to give them to Mob?

151
00:07:13,110 --> 00:07:15,470
But why, Onigawara-senpai?

152
00:07:16,900 --> 00:07:18,410
You better do this thing.

153
00:07:18,700 --> 00:07:20,130
He's so cool...

154
00:07:20,570 --> 00:07:22,370
Oh, those!

155
00:07:22,640 --> 00:07:24,600
So you ended up with them, Kageyama!

156
00:07:24,600 --> 00:07:27,340
The shoes Onigawara bought in the wrong size!

157
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,440
Did you have to open your big mouth?

158
00:07:31,800 --> 00:07:34,760
Spirits and Such Consultation Office

159
00:07:32,350 --> 00:07:34,760
Why are you so fidgety, Mob?

160
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:36,100
Reception

161
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:39,330
Oh, I'm just trying to exercise
any chance I get.

162
00:07:40,190 --> 00:07:42,150
Oh, so you're not fidgeting.

163
00:07:42,150 --> 00:07:44,940
He's got a marathon coming up.

164
00:07:44,940 --> 00:07:46,660
A marathon, huh?

165
00:07:46,960 --> 00:07:49,190
I always acted like I was sick.

166
00:07:49,540 --> 00:07:51,170
He's gonna try to place in the top ten

167
00:07:51,170 --> 00:07:53,740
and tell his beloved Tsubomi-chan how he feels.

168
00:07:55,270 --> 00:07:58,330
You're going to ask her out? Seriously?

169
00:08:04,750 --> 00:08:11,130
If you have
3 evil spirits,
the exorcism
fee on 1 of
them will be
on the house!!

170
00:08:06,280 --> 00:08:08,640
You don't have to come to work for a while.

171
00:08:08,640 --> 00:08:10,510
Huh? But why?

172
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:13,480
I'm probably not getting
any customers for a while anyway.

173
00:08:13,840 --> 00:08:17,460
More importantly, you should be
jogging to better prepare your body.

174
00:08:17,830 --> 00:08:18,970
All right, get changed.

175
00:08:19,340 --> 00:08:19,930
Huh?

176
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:23,660
We're going to get your legs accustomed
to the actual course you'll be running.

177
00:08:25,550 --> 00:08:27,940
Come on, lift those feet, Reigen!

178
00:08:27,940 --> 00:08:28,820
Shut up!

179
00:08:29,200 --> 00:08:32,980
I haven't... been exercising...
that much lately... myself!

180
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:34,780
I can't hear you!

181
00:08:36,670 --> 00:08:38,780
Hey, want to stop for some tea?

182
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:41,320
But we've only run about a
kilometer so far, Master.

183
00:08:43,460 --> 00:08:45,160
Huh? Nii-san?

184
00:08:45,160 --> 00:08:47,000
Hey, Ritsu.

185
00:08:47,210 --> 00:08:50,240
Dimple? Is he training for the marathon?

186
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:51,290
Yeah.

187
00:08:51,290 --> 00:08:55,200
Apparently, he's going to place in the
top ten and ask Tsubomi-chan out.

188
00:08:55,200 --> 00:08:55,970
What?!

189
00:08:56,300 --> 00:08:58,360
Takane Tsubomi-san?

190
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:01,210
I remember playing with her
when we were younger,

191
00:09:01,530 --> 00:09:04,440
but honestly, I found her
kind of hard to deal with.

192
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:08,900
I'm pretty sure I remember her going home
in the middle of hide-and-seek...

193
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:12,070
This makes me uneasy.

194
00:09:12,630 --> 00:09:15,170
I wonder if Nii-san will be okay...

195
00:09:16,390 --> 00:09:19,870
Shige! Wash your own dishes, will you?

196
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,230
Shige!

197
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:22,450
It's okay, Mom.

198
00:09:22,880 --> 00:09:24,330
I'll do it.

199
00:09:24,330 --> 00:09:27,920
You don't have to, Ritsu. You shouldn't
spoil your older brother like that.

200
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:29,630
Is something up?

201
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:32,340
Nii-san's working really hard lately,

202
00:09:32,800 --> 00:09:36,070
so I don't mind helping him just a bit.

203
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:45,270
Remember to take
2 breaths at once
Breathe in deeply, breathe out deeply
6-beat breathing style
Vertical

204
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:45,270
Stride
Longer strides
More damage
Faster speed, stamina...

205
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:45,270
Cadence
More rotations
Less damage
Uses more stamina

206
00:09:55,920 --> 00:09:57,820
Oh, hey, you two.
Thanks for coming by today.

207
00:09:57,820 --> 00:09:59,280
I look forward to working with you guys.

208
00:09:59,460 --> 00:10:01,270
I'm just doing this for my brother.

209
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:03,560
I want him to be able to
concentrate on training.

210
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:06,490
That said, we are subbing in for Kageyama-kun.

211
00:10:06,490 --> 00:10:08,000
I'll make sure I put my time in.

212
00:10:08,510 --> 00:10:10,940
Then, first, could you sort those files?

213
00:10:10,940 --> 00:10:14,090
Also, take a look at any
exorcism request emails.

214
00:10:14,470 --> 00:10:16,690
Hello? Are you open?

215
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:18,930
I didn't make a reservation or anything.

216
00:10:19,100 --> 00:10:20,740
Oh, I can see you immediately.

217
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:22,450
Please, have a seat.

218
00:10:22,450 --> 00:10:25,140
All right, go get some tea ready—

219
00:10:26,660 --> 00:10:28,460
Where'd the other kid go?

220
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:29,940
He seems to be hiding for some reason.

221
00:10:30,280 --> 00:10:31,410
Takane-san?!

222
00:10:31,410 --> 00:10:32,770
What is she doing here?

223
00:10:32,770 --> 00:10:34,320
I don't care about myself,

224
00:10:34,320 --> 00:10:38,860
but I can't let her find out Nii-san has
ties with a shady place like this.

225
00:10:38,860 --> 00:10:43,720
Um, I heard that you also
give relationship advice...

226
00:10:43,720 --> 00:10:44,610
Right?

227
00:10:44,610 --> 00:10:45,330
Yeah.

228
00:10:45,760 --> 00:10:47,330
Could you do that for us?

229
00:10:47,330 --> 00:10:49,040
Relationship advice?!

230
00:10:49,520 --> 00:10:51,980
If I could have you fill out
this questionnaire first.

231
00:10:51,980 --> 00:10:53,240
Oh, sure.

232
00:10:56,730 --> 00:10:59,840
I see. So you go to Salt Middle School.

233
00:11:00,230 --> 00:11:03,010
I actually know someone
at Salt Middle School.

234
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:05,760
Reigen! You shut your mouth!

235
00:11:05,760 --> 00:11:08,480
With our satisfied
customers

236
00:11:06,100 --> 00:11:08,480
What's this person like, Miki-chan?

237
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:12,480
Spirits and Such Consultation Office

238
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:11,580
Uh, could you let me do my job, please?

239
00:11:12,820 --> 00:11:14,010
I see...

240
00:11:14,010 --> 00:11:17,900
So this person is probably in your grade,
or maybe a bit older...

241
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:19,850
And they play some kind of sport.

242
00:11:19,850 --> 00:11:21,700
Wow! You're right!

243
00:11:23,190 --> 00:11:24,410
I see.

244
00:11:24,980 --> 00:11:28,720
He's on the soccer team,
so you want to get him some cleats.

245
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:31,670
But if you get him a really nice pair,

246
00:11:31,670 --> 00:11:34,760
their monetary value may leave
a bigger impression than your feelings.

247
00:11:32,880 --> 00:11:36,300
With our satisfied
customers

248
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:37,440
In that case, I think you
should start off as friends.

249
00:11:37,440 --> 00:11:40,370
Ask him what his hobbies
are outside of soccer,

250
00:11:40,370 --> 00:11:42,430
or about his favorite TV show...

251
00:11:43,070 --> 00:11:44,300
So basically,

252
00:11:44,660 --> 00:11:48,950
there's no need for you to rush in
and ask him out, Miki-san.

253
00:11:48,950 --> 00:11:50,270
In my opinion, at least.

254
00:11:50,270 --> 00:11:52,480
Okay! Thank you so much!

255
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,360
That was really helpful!

256
00:11:54,360 --> 00:11:58,480
Um, I didn't fill out the questionnaire,
but can I ask you some questions, too?

257
00:11:58,740 --> 00:12:00,280
Yes, of course!

258
00:12:00,280 --> 00:12:02,200
Did you want relationship advice as well?

259
00:12:02,400 --> 00:12:06,660
Yes. The person I like is someone from
another school who I meet at cram school.

260
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:08,830
Ah, I see.

261
00:12:08,830 --> 00:12:10,920
They talk to me all the time.

262
00:12:10,170 --> 00:12:11,790
Hey, what's with you, man?

263
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:15,660
Sometimes, we even walk home
together after cram school.

264
00:12:15,660 --> 00:12:17,420
Should I ask them out?

265
00:12:19,240 --> 00:12:23,740
Well, in that case, I think it'd be
fine to ask them out immediately.

266
00:12:23,740 --> 00:12:24,840
Hey!

267
00:12:24,840 --> 00:12:29,810
With our satisfied
customers

268
00:12:25,150 --> 00:12:29,810
From what you've told me, the other person
is obviously interested in you as well.

269
00:12:30,270 --> 00:12:33,520
If you ask them out, there's a very
good possibility they'll say yes.

270
00:12:33,790 --> 00:12:34,830
It's over...

271
00:12:34,830 --> 00:12:36,230
Okay.

272
00:12:36,640 --> 00:12:38,320
Thank you very much.

273
00:12:38,680 --> 00:12:40,440
Please come by again anytime.

274
00:12:40,740 --> 00:12:42,570
Do you know them, Little Bro?

275
00:12:42,570 --> 00:12:44,380
They looked older.

276
00:12:44,380 --> 00:12:46,410
Well, uh...

277
00:12:46,620 --> 00:12:47,880
I can't...

278
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:49,120
I can't tell Nii-san.

279
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:52,080
You can do this, Nii-san!

280
00:12:53,840 --> 00:12:56,350
I didn't know you went to
cram school, Tsubomi.

281
00:12:56,350 --> 00:12:57,840
You never mentioned that before.

282
00:12:57,840 --> 00:13:01,160
Nope. I just made it up.

283
00:13:01,490 --> 00:13:03,990
I didn't want you to get
scammed or something,

284
00:13:03,990 --> 00:13:05,800
so I thought I'd test him a little.

285
00:13:05,800 --> 00:13:08,980
Oh, really? I see.

286
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:11,770
And what did you think, Tsubomi?

287
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:14,730
Well...

288
00:13:19,120 --> 00:13:23,870
He didn't say anything wrong...
So he's probably okay.

289
00:13:24,490 --> 00:13:27,990
Mob Psycho

290
00:13:27,990 --> 00:13:31,490
Mob Psycho

291
00:13:31,490 --> 00:13:33,580
The Day of the Marathon

292
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:37,210
Salt Middle School Marathon

293
00:13:37,210 --> 00:13:38,620
You can do it!

294
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:40,090
My parents are here.

295
00:13:40,090 --> 00:13:41,500
Who's the fastest out of the guys?

296
00:13:42,010 --> 00:13:43,960
This day has finally arrived.

297
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:48,590
There are followers waiting
near the finish line.

298
00:13:49,210 --> 00:13:51,800
It's time to present their beloved leader.

299
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:53,600
You've got this, Mob-kun!

300
00:13:54,050 --> 00:13:57,070
I'm sure Ritsu will be fine,
but I'm a bit worried about Shigeo.

301
00:13:57,070 --> 00:13:59,780
Yeah. He's got the stamina of a snail.

302
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:03,070
We should watch from somewhere along
the course rather than the finish line.

303
00:14:03,070 --> 00:14:07,660
Nurse's Station

304
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:07,660
Salt MS

305
00:14:03,510 --> 00:14:04,760
Cough, cough.

306
00:14:04,760 --> 00:14:07,660
Oh, no. I've caught a cold.

307
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:09,020
Hack, hack.

308
00:14:07,660 --> 00:14:12,490
Visitor Station

309
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:11,280
Oh, did you catch a cold too, Kijibayashi-san?

310
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:12,490
So did I!

311
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:14,740
Wow, that's such a coincidence, Inukawa.

312
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:17,810
Horf, horf. Horf...

313
00:14:16,250 --> 00:14:19,660
You, too, Saruta? Not bad for a first-year.

314
00:14:19,660 --> 00:14:21,650
Oh, you're too kind.

315
00:14:21,650 --> 00:14:24,060
I learned a lot from the Telepathy Club.

316
00:14:24,060 --> 00:14:26,090
Run, you lazy bastards!

317
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:30,050
Salt MS

318
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:30,050
Inukawa

319
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:30,050
Salt MS

320
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:30,050
Kijibayashi

321
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:30,050
Salt MS

322
00:14:26,090 --> 00:14:30,050
Saruta

323
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:28,370
Even Mob-kun's going to run!

324
00:14:28,370 --> 00:14:30,050
So you three better get going, too!

325
00:14:30,520 --> 00:14:33,300
Shigeo! How ya doin'?

326
00:14:34,350 --> 00:14:37,530
He's doomed. He's super nervous.

327
00:14:39,020 --> 00:14:41,130
Shape up, Kageyama!

328
00:14:41,130 --> 00:14:42,020
President.

329
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,820
Show everyone the fruits of your training!

330
00:14:44,820 --> 00:14:46,650
We're rivals today!

331
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:48,160
Rivals...

332
00:14:48,160 --> 00:14:49,610
I'll do my best!

333
00:14:50,580 --> 00:14:52,620
Looks like he put those to good use.

334
00:14:52,870 --> 00:14:54,560
Way to go, shadow leader.

335
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:59,460
We will now begin the boys' race of
the Salt Middle School Marathon.

336
00:14:55,830 --> 00:14:59,790
Salt Middle School Marathon

337
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:13,490
On your marks...

338
00:15:13,490 --> 00:15:15,220
Ready...

339
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:28,450
Nii-san!

340
00:15:36,790 --> 00:15:38,250
Salt Middle School

341
00:15:45,390 --> 00:15:48,020
You're not catching up to
the leading pack on that leg...

342
00:15:48,380 --> 00:15:50,280
Want me to possess you?

343
00:15:50,280 --> 00:15:52,260
You just need to make the top ten, right?

344
00:15:55,280 --> 00:15:56,430
Figures.

345
00:15:58,840 --> 00:16:01,720
My kid looked so annoyed.

346
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:03,900
There's no way they'll catch up to the front.

347
00:16:04,190 --> 00:16:06,660
Ritsu passed by a long time ago.

348
00:16:08,400 --> 00:16:09,110
Shige!

349
00:16:10,300 --> 00:16:12,070
What happened to your leg?!

350
00:16:12,580 --> 00:16:14,870
But you built up your stamina, right?

351
00:16:14,870 --> 00:16:16,090
Hang in there!

352
00:16:16,090 --> 00:16:18,120
You're doing amazing!
You can do this, Shigeo!

353
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:20,660
Our boy has real guts now.

354
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:21,460
Yeah.

355
00:16:21,950 --> 00:16:24,780
I should make something yummy
for dinner tonight.

356
00:16:30,440 --> 00:16:31,720
Mob-kun.

357
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:33,780
You can d—

358
00:16:48,650 --> 00:16:50,380
His form's all wrong.

359
00:16:50,380 --> 00:16:52,120
Did he sprain something?

360
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:53,700
His pace is getting erratic, too.

361
00:16:56,590 --> 00:16:58,970
Hey, you've only got
about a kilometer to go.

362
00:16:58,970 --> 00:17:00,410
Move them legs!

363
00:17:00,610 --> 00:17:03,090
Reigen, you look like you're going all out.

364
00:17:03,090 --> 00:17:03,620
Don't look.

365
00:17:04,270 --> 00:17:08,210
I thought I'd help him keep
his pace toward the end,

366
00:17:08,540 --> 00:17:11,090
but the guys up front are way too fast.

367
00:17:11,660 --> 00:17:13,250
They're way ahead.

368
00:17:13,650 --> 00:17:16,050
I don't know if we can catch up
even if you sprint.

369
00:17:18,350 --> 00:17:21,810
I've been counting runners.
You're currently 74th.

370
00:17:21,810 --> 00:17:23,730
That's fantastic for Mob,

371
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:27,860
but for him to finish in the top ten,
he has to pass 64 others.

372
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,510
I see...

373
00:17:29,510 --> 00:17:30,820
Wanna get a taxi?

374
00:17:31,150 --> 00:17:33,740
I mean, the thought did cross my mind...

375
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:35,780
Don't be ridiculous. Look at that face.

376
00:17:36,370 --> 00:17:38,490
I'm pretty sure he hasn't given up yet.

377
00:17:58,030 --> 00:18:00,390
Kageyama, you're awake?

378
00:18:01,510 --> 00:18:03,740
You should never push yourself too far.

379
00:18:03,740 --> 00:18:04,850
Sensei...

380
00:18:05,330 --> 00:18:08,060
That marathon's over, huh?

381
00:18:08,470 --> 00:18:09,340
Yeah...

382
00:18:09,670 --> 00:18:13,780
Oh, your younger brother managed to
overtake some third-years and place 9th.

383
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:15,320
I see.

384
00:18:16,160 --> 00:18:17,130
Ritsu...

385
00:18:18,820 --> 00:18:22,580
Kageyama, you used to seem a bit glum,

386
00:18:22,940 --> 00:18:24,860
but you're much brighter now.

387
00:18:24,860 --> 00:18:25,540
Pardon?

388
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,390
Do you need someone to come get you?

389
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:30,500
No, I can go home myself.

390
00:18:34,400 --> 00:18:35,460
He hasn't shown up...

391
00:18:35,620 --> 00:18:38,780
Yeah... Where in the world is our leader?

392
00:18:47,220 --> 00:18:48,560
Well, you're in a good mood.

393
00:18:48,560 --> 00:18:50,610
Of course I am.

394
00:18:50,610 --> 00:18:54,570
We're celebrating Ritsu placing 9th,
and Shige running the whole nine.

395
00:18:54,570 --> 00:18:55,730
What the heck?

396
00:18:57,970 --> 00:19:00,700
I'll get it. I wonder if it's Nii-san.

397
00:19:01,070 --> 00:19:04,550
Koga-sensei just called saying
he left school a little while ago.

398
00:19:04,870 --> 00:19:07,410
I'm glad he just had mild anemia.

399
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:17,090
Heya.

400
00:19:18,190 --> 00:19:19,300
You're...

401
00:19:20,260 --> 00:19:21,260
the one from...

402
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,470
How did you find this place?

403
00:19:25,810 --> 00:19:28,350
Didn't I say I'd be seeing you again?

404
00:19:28,350 --> 00:19:30,290
Who is it? A friend of yours?

405
00:19:30,290 --> 00:19:30,940
Mom!

406
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:33,150
Don't come over here right now!

407
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:35,950
Oh... Now I see.

408
00:19:35,950 --> 00:19:38,870
Your parents are here, too.
I guess I shouldn't be surprised.

409
00:19:38,870 --> 00:19:40,610
Well, this complicates things.

410
00:19:41,810 --> 00:19:44,340
Hey, what do you mean by—

411
00:19:54,480 --> 00:19:55,700
What is that?

412
00:19:57,330 --> 00:20:00,200
I wonder what's going on.
There's smoke over there.

413
00:20:00,480 --> 00:20:01,380
Is there a fire?

414
00:20:01,800 --> 00:20:02,800
Wait...

415
00:20:03,360 --> 00:20:05,080
Isn't that where...

416
00:20:15,170 --> 00:20:18,730
Apparently, there was
a sudden explosion of fire.

417
00:20:18,750 --> 00:20:20,540
They said it might've been an arsonist.

418
00:20:24,330 --> 00:20:27,260
Nobody knows if the family got to safety.

419
00:20:27,650 --> 00:20:29,570
Oh, you're one of the Kageyama boys.

420
00:20:29,570 --> 00:20:31,900
Thank goodness you're safe.

421
00:20:32,550 --> 00:20:34,120
H-Hey, wait! Pull yourself together!

422
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:35,290
You can't go any closer!

423
00:20:35,290 --> 00:20:37,820
Someone, please stop him!

424
00:20:37,820 --> 00:20:38,590
That's dangerous!

425
00:20:38,590 --> 00:20:40,260
He went into the fire!

426
00:20:41,300 --> 00:20:44,950
It's okay... Dad was home today.

427
00:20:46,230 --> 00:20:48,470
Dad can be a bit strict at times,

428
00:20:48,840 --> 00:20:50,930
but he's strong and reliable.

429
00:20:51,380 --> 00:20:55,150
He even took the day off from
work today to watch me run.

430
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:59,610
And Mom's always careful with the stove.

431
00:21:00,270 --> 00:21:03,730
When I was younger, she yelled at me
for messing around with fireworks.

432
00:21:04,420 --> 00:21:06,490
Not to mention, Ritsu's here.

433
00:21:07,340 --> 00:21:10,200
He's my brilliant younger brother
who's always calm.

434
00:21:10,810 --> 00:21:13,370
It's okay. It'll be okay.

435
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:15,670
It's too bad that our home is burning down,

436
00:21:16,430 --> 00:21:18,380
but as long as we're together,
we can start over.

437
00:21:21,450 --> 00:21:22,730
There's no one here?

438
00:21:23,280 --> 00:21:25,520
They must've gotten away, then!

439
00:21:25,520 --> 00:21:26,510
Shigeo!

440
00:21:26,930 --> 00:21:29,100
There were signs of a struggle
at the front door.

441
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:31,560
Someone must've forced their way in!

442
00:21:31,760 --> 00:21:34,520
Someone did this...?

443
00:21:34,870 --> 00:21:36,770
H-Hang on a sec.

444
00:21:37,200 --> 00:21:40,730
Does that mean someone
could've taken them, too?

445
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:44,740
I have to look for clues!

446
00:21:53,030 --> 00:21:54,570
Close your eyes!

447
00:21:54,570 --> 00:21:57,460
Don't look, Shigeo!

448
00:22:36,680 --> 00:22:41,700
I spilled a seed and lost sight of it

449
00:22:45,420 --> 00:22:50,720
I'll find it using the color it's dyed in and watch it grow

450
00:22:53,060 --> 00:22:59,190
It immediately returned to the palm of my hand

451
00:22:59,190 --> 00:23:08,760
But it's still too light and too frail to reach for the skies

452
00:23:09,820 --> 00:23:14,380
The world coldly drains away all the heat

453
00:23:14,380 --> 00:23:18,930
The bright sunshine just isn't enough

454
00:23:18,930 --> 00:23:23,320
The memories are closing off what lies ahead

455
00:23:23,320 --> 00:23:28,420
Shake off their warmth and set off into the distance

456
00:23:29,680 --> 00:23:35,180
If I let it wither, it'd be over just like that

457
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:40,470
But my hope just doesn't fade away

458
00:23:55,520 --> 00:23:58,780
The super dangerous esper organization,
Claw, attacks Seasoning City!

459
00:23:58,780 --> 00:24:00,240
The boss, the upper echelon,
and the foreigner squad...

460
00:24:00,240 --> 00:24:03,500
It appears that I, Reigen Arataka,
must make a stand!

461
00:24:03,500 --> 00:24:05,590
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 II Episode 9:

462
00:24:05,590 --> 00:24:06,960
"Show Me What You've Got ~Band Together~."

463
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:09,770
Illegal downloads?
Do you want to be cursed?

464
00:24:06,960 --> 00:24:10,260
Show Me What You've Got
~Band Together~
